# Scaffold manifest
#
# Consumed by the scaffold copier (`.agents/scripts/install-scaffold.sh`) to install this
# cross-agent governance scaffold into a target project. One entry per line, relative to
# the repository root. A trailing "/" copies that directory recursively. Blank lines and
# lines starting with "#" are ignored.
#
# ## Ownership directives
#
# A line reading `# @owner scaffold` or `# @owner project` applies to every entry below it
# until the next such line, and declares who wins when the target's copy and this one have
# diverged (ADR-0019). It is a comment, so every reader that predates it — including
# `verify-scaffold.sh` §6 — sees the manifest it has always seen.
#
#   scaffold  the scaffold authors the file and a project is not meant to rewrite it, so an
#             upstream change must reach the target: it is updated when the target never
#             touched it, and conflict-marked when both sides moved.
#   project   the scaffold only seeds the file and the project fills it in, so a divergent
#             destination is left exactly as it is.
#
# Project-owned is the default for anything not covered by a directive: it is the copier's
# historical behavior, so an unclassified entry cannot regress into being overwritten.

# @owner project
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore
.env.mcp.example
.mcp.json
opencode.json
# The project's own vocabulary, its own invariants (ADR-0021), the generated index (which carries
# the project's terms once it has any), and the changelog the project appends to. The two
# scaffold-owned family members — vocabulary and invariants — are in the block below; the split by
# owner is what ADR-0017 and ADR-0021 exist for.
.agents/ubiquitous-language.md
.agents/ubiquitous-language-index.md
.agents/ubiquitous-language-changelog.md
.agents/ubiquitous-language-invariants.md
.agents/labels.md
.agents/plans/.gitkeep
.agents/specs/.gitkeep
.agents/adr/.gitkeep
.agents/harness.config.example

# @owner scaffold
.agents/ubiquitous-language-invariants-scaffold.md
.agents/ubiquitous-language-scaffold.md
.agents/rules/
.agents/commands/
.agents/scripts/
.agents/skills/
# The workflow guide documents this harness's own commands and gates; a project
# adopts it rather than writes it, so an upstream correction has to be able to land.
.agents/docs/
# Harness-level decisions every scaffolded project inherits — the skills layout is cited by
# .agents/rules/skill-creation.md, the handoff sandbox by .agents/commands/handoff.md, the
# vendoring policy by both AGENTS.md and .agents/rules/skill-creation.md, 0004-0008 by
# .agents/rules/parallel-orchestration.md, and 0009-0013 by
# .agents/commands/review-branch.md, and 0014-0015 by both. 0016-0022 govern the glossary
# family and the copier's sync semantics. Where a project's own ADRs start is open: see below.
# 0023 (local mode) and 0024 (product content) are provisional: they collide with project ADRs
# already numbered 0023 or 0024 in consumers, so scaffold ADR numbering is settled by its own
# /grill before any consumer is synced past this point (.agents/specs/2026-10-15-local-mode.md,
# decision 19).
.agents/adr/0001-skills-canonical-in-agents-skills.md
.agents/adr/0002-handoff-shares-the-working-tree.md
.agents/adr/0003-vendored-artifacts-carry-no-attribution.md
.agents/adr/0004-runner-is-sole-writer-of-the-epic-branch.md
.agents/adr/0005-review-state-derived-from-git.md
.agents/adr/0006-supervised-execution-is-a-command-not-a-flag.md
.agents/adr/0007-one-pipeline-for-both-execution-paths.md
.agents/adr/0008-corpus-pack-shares-inputs-not-findings.md
.agents/adr/0009-interactive-review-diffs-the-working-tree.md
.agents/adr/0010-interactive-gate-procedure-lives-in-the-command.md
.agents/adr/0011-review-report-overwrites-headless-appends-interactively.md
.agents/adr/0012-interactive-reviewer-runs-under-review-agent-exec-cmd.md
.agents/adr/0013-interactive-gate-builds-a-corpus-pack-too.md
.agents/adr/0014-one-reviewer-process-per-axis.md
.agents/adr/0015-issue-labels-are-informational.md
.agents/adr/0016-always-on-is-the-index-and-the-invariants.md
.agents/adr/0017-scaffold-and-product-vocabulary-have-owners.md
.agents/adr/0018-the-glossary-has-a-byte-budget.md
.agents/adr/0019-install-scaffold-syncs-instead-of-skipping.md
.agents/adr/0020-unmarkable-divergence-is-marked-beside-the-path.md
